      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        247.0312042236328,
        558.0000610351562,
        256.79217529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "network with FiLM conditioning [41], as in [1]. All simu-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        259.1456298828125,
        558.0008544921875,
        268.05218505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lations ran on a desktop computer with an NVIDIA RTX",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        271.10064697265625,
        558.0008544921875,
        280.0072021484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4070 (12 GB) GPU. When evaluating trained policies, we",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        283.056640625,
        558.0007934570312,
        291.96319580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "use MuJoCo CPU (64-bit) rather than MJX (32-bit), resulting",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        295.0116271972656,
        558.0008544921875,
        303.9181823730469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in a small sim-to-sim gap.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        306.96661376953125,
        420.9155578613281,
        315.8731689453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A. Policy Performance",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        328.39227294921875,
        406.12115478515625,
        336.98004150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Footage of closed-loop GPC performance on each of the",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        344.4886169433594,
        558.00146484375,
        353.3951721191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "examples is shown in the accompanying video (https:",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        356.4446105957031,
        558.0007934570312,
        365.3511657714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "//youtu.be/mjL7CF877Ow). To evaluate performance",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        368.39959716796875,
        558.0013427734375,
        377.30615234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "quantitatively, we perform 100 randomly-initialized simu-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        380.3545837402344,
        558.0007934570312,
        389.2611389160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lations and record the average cost per time step as a",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        392.3095703125,
        558.0007934570312,
        401.21612548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance metric. Figure 3a compares our approach (GPC,",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        404.2645568847656,
        558.0009765625,
        413.1711120605469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "GPC+) with PPO and SPC baselines. For PPO training, we",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        416.21954345703125,
        558.0010986328125,
        425.1260986328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "use the same cost (negative reward), network size, batch size,",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        428.175537109375,
        558.0009155273438,
        437.08209228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and total number of simulation time steps3 as GPC. SPC and",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        436.5145263671875,
        558.000732421875,
        449.0370788574219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "GPC+ both use N = 128 rollouts. Interestingly, GPC and",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        451.9261169433594,
        558.0107421875,
        460.9920654296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "GPC+ perform on par or better than PPO with the same",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        463.9209289550781,
        558.0009765625,
        472.8773193359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "amount of training data. Of course, further hyperparameter",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        475.87591552734375,
        558.0009155273438,
        484.90203857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and reward tuning could improve both PPO and GPC perfor-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        487.9504699707031,
        558.0009765625,
        496.8570251464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mance: a systematic hyperparameter sensitivity comparison",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        499.9064636230469,
        558.0009765625,
        508.8130187988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is left for future work.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        511.8614501953125,
        405.3439025878906,
        520.7680053710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 3b compares our warm-start strategy with action",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        524.12841796875,
        558.0012817382812,
        533.0349731445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "inpainting [27], both using the same GPC policy. For action",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        536.08447265625,
        558.0009155273438,
        544.9910278320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "inpainting, we use the soft-masking pseudoinverse guidance",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        548.0394287109375,
        558.0008544921875,
        556.9459838867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "strategy of [27, Eq. 2-4]. Interestingly, action inpainting—a",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        559.9944458007812,
        558.0007934570312,
        568.9010009765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state-of-the-art method for temporal consistency enforcement",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        571.949462890625,
        558.0009765625,
        580.8560180664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in behavior cloning—degrades performance on these high-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        583.9044189453125,
        558.0009155273438,
        592.8109741210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "frequency tasks. This is likely because action inpainting is",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        595.8594360351562,
        558.0009155273438,
        604.7659912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "designed for relatively slow, quasi-static tasks with signifi-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        607.8154296875,
        558.0007934570312,
        616.7219848632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cant inference delays. In contrast, GPC inference times range",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        619.7704467773438,
        558.0009155273438,
        628.677001953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
